#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A stand-in `pohunek` CLI with synthetic sessions on three hosts.

Point the widget at it to try the panel without a daemon, or to take
screenshots that show no real work:

    omarchy bar set pohunek.sessions command ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/pohunek.sessions/tools/demo-pohunek

and back with `omarchy bar set pohunek.sessions command pohunek`. Answers the
read commands the widget uses and the commands tools/onboard calls; anything
else prints what it would do.

The onboarding answers follow pohunek 0.42.0 (zajca/pohunek tag v0.42.0); the
source of each document is named where it is built. Optional environment, used
by tests/onboard_test.py:

  DEMO_POHUNEK_LOG        file under $TMPDIR: one JSON line per call; also makes
                          unknown commands and flags a usage error (exit 2)
  DEMO_POHUNEK_STATE      directory under $TMPDIR for installed packages, the
                          onboard session and the service install
  DEMO_POHUNEK_VERSION    version `--version` reports (default 0.42.0)
  DEMO_POHUNEK_ASSISTANT  assistant entry of the setup plan: gap (default),
                          install or present
  DEMO_POHUNEK_SERVICE    `install` plans a fresh service install until
                          `setup --yes` ran; otherwise the service is present
  DEMO_POHUNEK_NO_HOOKS   1: `setup` does not know `--hooks` (a core before 0.42)
  DEMO_POHUNEK_EXTRA_PROBLEM  1: `setup --yes` also fails a doctor check
"""
